program	enum_ref_payload_escape.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	Parse error at 13:18: payload `r` of case `Held` in enum `Slot` may not be a reference: its type `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). An enum value is storage that outlives every call that could have created the reference, so the pointer it holds outlives what it names. Store the value instead (`r: Int`), or — to hand out storage this type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out
